Faced with the problem of “how to improve the morning routine from waking up to arriving at school,” we can apply the four methods of computational thinking. First, decompose the problem by breaking the process into independent steps such as getting up, washing, having breakfast,and heading out. Second, use pattern recognition by recording data over several days to identify which steps take the longest or are most prone to delay. Third, use abstraction focusing only on the fixed time and dependencies among steps (for example, heating breakfast can be done while washing). Finally, design an frame that sets a  time limit for each step and finish this tasks in a logical order, creating a sueful work frame to ensure you arrive at school on time every day.
